{"step_index":338,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:35:02Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-07T07:35:02+01:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-07T07:35:02+01:00\nShowing lines 1-100 of 163\n1: # 🛡️ AegisShield EDR - Cyber Process Monitor & Threat Eradicator\n2: \n3: > **Advanced Real-Time Spyware, Antivirus, Remote Desktop Control (LOLRMM), Process Monitor, Network Origin Tracer, Access Control & Trojan Detection Dashboard**\n4: > *Scans your system, identifies threats via multi-vector heuristics and threat intelligence, audits network connections, enforces allow/block rules, dispatches email reports, and kills threats with a single click.*\n5: \n6: ---\n7: \n8: ## 🌟 Key Features\n9: \n10: ### 1. 🛡️ Access Control & Allow / Block Policy Engine\n11: * **Allowlist (Whitelist):** Explicitly trust processes by **Name**, **Executable Path**, or **SHA256 Hash**. Whitelisted software is assigned a Threat Score of 0, alerts are suppressed, and it is exempt from termination.\n12: * **Blocklist (Blacklist):** Ban known malicious processes or scripts. Any process matching a blacklist rule is flagged as `CRITICAL` (Score: 100) and can be immediately eradicated.\n13: * **IP Banning & Windows Firewall Integration:** Ban suspicious remote IP addresses. AegisShield creates outbound rules in Windows Firewall (`netsh advfirewall firewall add rule ...`) and flags any process attempting communication with banned IPs.\n14: * **Quick UI Actions:** 1-click **Allow** and **Block** buttons located on every process row and threat card.\n15: \n16: ### 2. 🌐 Network Radar & IP Origin Tracer\n17: * **Network Process Auditing:** Discovers exactly which processes are using network sockets, mapping local ports to remote IP endpoints.\n18: * **Origin & Geolocation Tracing:** Resolves remote IPs using reverse DNS (PTR records) and geographic lookup (Country, Organization, ISP, and ASN).\n19: * **Genuineness & Reputation Classification:** Automatically assesses whether an endpoint is legitimate:\n20:   * 🟢 **`GENUINE CLOUD / CDN`**: Verified major tech infrastructure (Microsoft/Azure, Google/GCP, Cloudflare, Amazon AWS, Apple, Akamai, GitHub, Fastly).\n21:   * 🔵 **`PRIVATE LAN`**: Safe local subnet (`192.168.x.x`, `10.x.x.x`, `172.16-31.x.x`, `127.0.0.1`).\n22:   * 🔴 **`SUSPICIOUS C2 / RAT PORT`**: Communication on known Trojan/RAT ports (`1177`, `1604`, `2404`, `4444`, `4782`, `5555`, `6606`, etc.) or cryptocurrency mining pools.\n23:   * ⚪ **`UNVERIFIED EXTERNAL`**: General public internet hosts requiring administrative scrutiny.\n24: * **Interactive Actions:** One-click `Block IP` (Windows Firewall rule) and `Deep Trace` drawer for full ASN & network telemetry.\n25: \n26: ### 3. 📧 Automated & On-Demand Email Security Reports\n27: * **Configurable SMTP Dispatch:** Supports Gmail (App Passwords), Outlook, Microsoft 365, or custom corporate SMTP relays with TLS / SSL encryption.\n28: * **Executive HTML Security Reports:** Formats rich, styled HTML reports including:\n29:   * Health index, scan timestamp, and host metrics.\n30:   * Detected threats table 